  "arrangerNotes": "9/8 time (eighth = 0.5 beat). Verse 1 and refrain verified against the LilyPond score on English Wikipedia. Simplification: the chromatic G♯ lower neighbour in 'glory divine' (A–G♯–A) is played as 4 (G), since tongue drums have no chromatic notes. D drum: as written (range low 7 to high 2), D minLayout 13. C drum: the C drum has no high 2, so the line 'this is my story, this is my song' in the second half of the refrain (score events 56–64) is played one octave lower; C minLayout 11. C and D arrangements differ where noted above (each fits its own drum).",
  "verified": true
